      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this bright and spacious four-bedroom mid-terrace family home to the market in the ever-popular Buttercup Drive, Darndale, Dublin 17. Tucked away in a quiet cul-de-sac and enjoying a private position that is not overlooked to the front, No. 11 offers an excellent opportunity for first-time buyers, growing families and investors alike.\n\nThe location is second to none with every conceivable amenity within easy reach including local primary and secondary schools, shops, supermarkets, cafés, sporting facilities and parks. The area is well served by excellent public transport links, while the M50, M1, Dublin Airport, Beaumont Hospital and Northside Shopping Centre are all easily accessible, making this a highly convenient location for commuters.\n\nBright and well-proportioned internal living accommodation extending to c. 89 sq.m comprises of an entrance hallway, a spacious living room with feature fireplace and double doors leading to a generous open-plan kitchen/dining area with direct access to the covered rear courtyard. Upstairs you will find four well-proportioned bedrooms and a fully tiled family shower room.\n\nTo the front, the property benefits from a gated driveway providing valuable off-street parking together with ample on-street parking. To the rear is a low-maintenance covered courtyard, offering a private outdoor space that can be enjoyed throughout the year.\n\nNo. 11 comes to the market in good condition throughout and, with no onward chain, is ready for its next owner. Early interest is expected, so contact Ray Cooke Auctioneers today on 0868323302 or 015411455 to arrange a viewing.\n\nFeatures\n• c. 89 sq.m\n• BER C2\n• Gas-fired central heating\n• Bright and spacious living accommodation\n• Large open-plan kitchen/dining area\n• Spacious living room with feature fireplace\n• Fully tiled modern shower room\n• Covered rear courtyard\n• Gated driveway with off-street parking\n• Ample on-street parking\n• PVC double glazed windows\n• Quiet cul-de-sac setting\n• Not overlooked to the front\n• No onward chain\n• Fantastic opportunity for first-time buyers, families and investors\n• Excellent transport links nearby\n• Viewing highly recommended\n"
      },
      {
